<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.3 · Sailing, Combat & the Kingdom" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-3" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.3</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Sailing, Combat & the Kingdom</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Start the kingdom's passive resources, close the lighthouse prerequisite for Recipe for Disaster, then learn Sailing as a new activity rather than a list of coordinates. The route stops at actual 45 Sailing and actual 40+ Slayer; its next Slayer gate belongs later.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Complete Throne of Miscellania and Royal Trouble, with a visible actual-40 Slayer checkpoint between them. Finish Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl and Horror from the Deep before the 2.4 Recipe for Disaster block. Learn Sailing through Pandemonium, Prying Times and Current Affairs, then reach actual 45."
        stats={["Actual 40 Slayer before Royal Trouble", "Actual 12 Sailing before Prying Times", "Actual 22 Sailing before Current Affairs", "Actual 45 Sailing at exit; 51 Slayer is deferred"]}
        unlocks={["Kingdom coffer and 15-worker post-Royal resource engine", "Horror from the Deep / RFD prerequisite closed", "Raft, skiff option, Captain's log and charting tools", "Sailing ready for later Troubled Tortugans"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Starting point:</strong> 2.2 finished Heroes' Quest, Monkey Madness I and Daero's <strong>35,000 Attack/Defence + 20,000 Strength/Hitpoints</strong> reward. The Fremennik Trials and The Knight's Sword were finished in Chapter 1. Do not assume the optional Chapter 1 65/65/65 melee block. Check live levels when choosing a combat style or wielding Iban's staff (u), which needs 50 Attack and 50 Magic.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Start the passive engine</div><h2>Claim the kingdom now, then feed its workers.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i23-throne" number="1" title="Complete Throne of Miscellania">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Heroes' Quest and The Fremennik Trials are complete, so nothing useful is gained by leaving this passive system dormant. Take the Rellekka longboat to Miscellania, or fairy ring <strong>CIP</strong> if available. Managing Miscellania means placing coins in a kingdom coffer, assigning workers to resources and occasionally restoring approval; the workers then gather materials over real time.</p>
        <p><strong>Bring/check:</strong> an <strong>iron bar</strong>, one ordinary <strong>log</strong> (or cut one on the island), and a common <strong>ring</strong> for the royal-family conversation; a gold ring is easy to make or bank. Flowers and a bow can speed the princess route, but are not mandatory—mixed flowers are sold in the castle courtyard. Bring an axe for approval and a little travel cash. Speak to King Vargas, earn the chosen child's trust, carry the anthem/treaty between the two courts, and have Derrik make the giant nib from your iron bar before signing.</p>
        <p>The quest needs <strong>75% public support</strong> to finish, starting near 25%. Chop the island's <strong>maple trees</strong> for a simple, low-attention approval loop; your 70 Woodcutting easily clears it. Fishing, coal mining or raking also work. Workers thank you as approval rises; check with Advisor Ghrim, and stop once the 75% quest gate is satisfied. Do not individually buy scores of flowers just to minimize clicks on a map. Finish with Vargas. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Throne_of_Miscellania" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest details</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-first-kingdom" number="2" title="Fund and assign the first ten kingdom workers">
        <p>Speak to <strong>Advisor Ghrim</strong> after the quest. Put roughly <strong>1,000,000 coins</strong> in the coffer if the 2.1 battlestaff cash reserve permits; <strong>500,000</strong> is the minimum balance for the current maximum <strong>50,000 gp daily draw</strong>. If cash is tighter, deposit what you can and top up from later alchs rather than postponing the unlock. This spends GP for account resources, not for Grand Exchange profit.</p>
        <p>Assign all <strong>ten available workers to herbs</strong>. The route still needs <strong>70 Herblore</strong>, so this starts a valuable, resource-gated supply early. Keep approval reasonably high: it falls by about <strong>2.5 percentage points per day</strong> before Royal Trouble. Revisit when convenient, chop a few maples or use another nearby approval action, and let the system run while you do Slayer. There is no daily alarm or requirement to collect every day. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Managing_Miscellania" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki coffer and worker mechanics</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-slayer-40" number="3" title="Train Slayer from the current level to actual 40">
        <p><strong>Why 40:</strong> Royal Trouble requires it now; the Chapter 1 handoff was only about 20+. Check the actual skill tab, take ordinary Slayer tasks, and stop at <strong>unboosted 40</strong>. This is not a 51-Slayer grind for Troubled Tortugans yet.</p>
        <p><strong>Default master:</strong> <strong>Vannaka</strong> in Edgeville Dungeon, east of the Wilderness gate, accepts combat level 40+. An Edgeville teleport or fairy ring <strong>DKR</strong> brings you near the dungeon; speak to him for an assignment, check the monster and location in the Slayer interface, bank for food/prayer/teleports, then kill the assigned number and return for another task. A higher master is fine only if your <em>observed</em> combat level supports it comfortably. Task sequence and XP vary by RNG. You do not need a cannon, burst runes or a special task list.</p>
        <p>Check each monster's required gear before leaving: for example, <strong>earmuffs for banshees</strong> and a <strong>mirror shield for cockatrices/basilisks</strong>; Slayer masters sell many such items. Save points where possible. If an assignment is truly miserable, a normal cancellation costs <strong>30 Slayer points</strong> when you have them; asking Turael in Burthorpe to replace a task is an emergency escape but <strong>resets the normal task streak</strong>. Do not reset a valuable streak for routine inconvenience. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Slayer" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki masters, equipment and task mechanics</a>.</p>
        <p>Use the combat XP deliberately: check post-2.2 Attack/Strength/Defence, then use an appropriate style to advance whichever later gate is lagging—<strong>Attack + Strength 130</strong> for Warriors' Guild, actual <strong>60 Defence</strong> to equip the dragon defender, then <strong>65/70 Defence</strong> for King's Ransom/Piety. If you already did optional 65/65/65, use your preferred style. No exact post-task melee level is presumed.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i23-slayer-choices" informational={true} skill="Slayer" target="actual 40" why="The Royal Trouble gate is the only mandatory stop here; task RNG determines the journey." recommended="Ordinary Vannaka tasks with a bank trip and gear check per assignment; use melee styles to make progress on the combat stat you actually need." relaxed="Take breaks between tasks, use food and protection prayers on awkward monsters, and choose a familiar eligible master if Vannaka's pool feels poor." fast="A stronger master or faster combat setup is optional if your real levels and supplies support it; no cannon/burst purchase is budgeted." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-royal-trouble" number="4" title="Complete Royal Trouble at actual 40 Slayer">
        <p>Return to Miscellania with <strong>actual 40 Slayer and 40 Agility</strong> (Agility is already well above this). Bring a <strong>pickaxe</strong>, <strong>five coal</strong> if banked, <strong>two ropes</strong> if banked, food, antipoison, prayer restore, a teleport and Magic/Ranged combat supplies. Coal and rope can also be obtained during the quest. The later <strong>level-149 Giant Sea Snake</strong> is the dangerous part: rebank before the tunnel, use protection prayer, antipoison and distance where possible, and follow the cave route rather than taking a minimal-food gamble. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Royal_Trouble" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki tunnel and snake walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <p>Finish the quest before collecting kingdom output. It awards <strong>5,000 XP each in Slayer, Agility and Hitpoints</strong> and improves the kingdom. Read your <em>actual</em> Slayer level afterward; the reward is not a hidden promise that you reached a later gate.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-improved-kingdom" number="5" title="Set the improved kingdom to fifteen useful workers">
        <p>Royal Trouble raises the workforce to <strong>15</strong> and the maximum coffer draw to <strong>75,000 gp per day</strong>. Maintain at least <strong>750,000 gp</strong> for full daily spending; a comfortable balance is roughly <strong>1.5–2 million</strong> if the 2.1 cash engine permits. Top up when collecting or passing through, not on a rigid daily schedule. Approval now falls about <strong>1 percentage point per day</strong>; restore it periodically with maple chopping or another easy island task.</p>
        <p><strong>Default allocation: ten herbs + five hardwood/teak workers.</strong> Herbs support the later 70-Herblore bottleneck; teak logs can become planks for the later 70-Construction block. Check your leftover 2.1 teak stock before committing: if Construction is well supplied but seeds/nests would help Farming, move those five workers to <strong>maples</strong> instead. The allocation is adjustable, including before collection, and no workers should sit idle. It is an Ironman resource decision, not a fixed GE-profit formula. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Managing_Miscellania" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki resource categories and collection</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Close the RFD lighthouse dependency</div><h2>A short pub circuit leads directly to Horror from the Deep.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i23-barcrawl" number="6" title="Finish Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl completely">
        <p><strong>Why:</strong> Horror from the Deep needs the Barcrawl, and full Recipe for Disaster needs Horror. Go to the <strong>Barbarian Outpost</strong> (games necklace), talk to the <strong>Barbarian guard</strong> at the agility-course gate and take the barcrawl card. Alfred Grimhand is the namesake of the challenge, not this starting guard. Carry the card, about <strong>1,000 coins</strong>, food and your normal teleports. Ask each bartender for the special drink; ordinary beer does not stamp the card. Some drinks drain stats or Hitpoints, especially the Ardougne Heart Stopper, so heal between pubs and do not combine this with a boss trip.</p>
        <p>Use a compact regional circuit, in whichever direction your teleports favor: <strong>Seers' Forester's Arms → Ardougne Flying Horse → Yanille Dragon Inn → Brimhaven Dead Man's Chest and Musa Point Karamja Spirits → Port Sarim Rusty Anchor and Falador Rising Sun → Varrock Blue Moon and Jolly Boar → Grand Tree Blurberry Bar</strong>. That is the ten required pubs, not ten copies of one drink. Check every stamp on the card, then return to the <strong>Barbarian guard</strong> at the Outpost for the completed miniquest and agility-course access. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Alfred_Grimhand%27s_Barcrawl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki pub list and drink effects</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-horror" number="7" title="Complete Horror from the Deep and choose a damaged god book">
        <p><strong>Requirements:</strong> completed Barcrawl and 35 Agility, already covered. Start with <strong>Larrissa</strong> at the Lighthouse north of the Barbarian Outpost; fairy ring <strong>ALP</strong> reaches the island if unlocked. Withdraw <strong>two ordinary planks, 60 steel nails, hammer, molten glass, swamp tar and tinderbox</strong> for the bridge and lamp. Chapter 1 deliberately banked spare molten glass—use one instead of making a fresh batch. Bring <strong>one each of air, fire, water and earth runes</strong>, any <strong>sword or longsword</strong> you can sacrifice, and one normal <strong>arrow</strong> (not a bolt/training/ogre arrow) for the sealed door. These are consumed; do not sacrifice prized gear. Add elemental combat runes, Magic/Ranged/melee gear, food, prayer restore, antipoison and a teleport.</p>
        <p>Repair the bridge, fetch the Lighthouse key from <strong>Gunnjorn</strong> inside the Barbarian Outpost course, repair/light the mechanism, then feed the six door symbols their items. The first Dagannoth is a warm-up. The <strong>Dagannoth Mother</strong> changes colour and only the matching damage type works: <strong>white air, blue water, brown earth, red fire, green Ranged, orange melee</strong>. Bring all four elemental spells and a ranged/melee switch, change attack when she changes, and use food/prayer rather than tanking. If a phase is awkward, survive until it changes; the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Horror_from_the_Deep" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki fight guide</a> has exact positioning.</p>
        <p>Open the rusty casket with <strong>Jossik</strong> and choose a damaged book. <strong>Zamorak's unholy book</strong> is a sensible offensive first choice if you later find its clue-scroll pages; Saradomin or Guthix is fine for your preferred future bonus. The damaged book itself gives a useful <strong>+5 Prayer</strong>; completing any book needs four specific pages and is <em>not</em> required. Jossik can sell other damaged books later. Bank the book and verify the quest complete: it gives <strong>4,662.5 XP each in Magic, Strength and Ranged</strong>, Lighthouse/Dagannoth access, and closes RFD's Horror prerequisite.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <ExpandableNote label="Optional combat detours" title="Barbarian Assault can wait; Dagannoth Rex is deferred">
        <p><strong>Barbarian Assault is optional.</strong> At the Barbarian Outpost, a <strong>five-player team</strong> covers Attacker, Defender, Collector and Healer roles through ten waves, then coordinates a queen kill. One queen kill and <strong>375 honour points in each role</strong> allow you to buy the <strong>fighter torso</strong>, a strong melee body; learning roles and forming teams can take a few hours. The queen run also serves the later Kandarin hard diary if you choose that diary. Neither the torso nor granite body is a quest, defender or Piety gate. If you enjoy group minigames, do it now or later, then rejoin at Step 8 with no missing mandatory XP or item. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Barbarian_Assault" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki roles and rewards</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Dagannoth Rex is deferred.</strong> Horror opens the Lighthouse area, and the selected 2.2 Attack XP should make Iban's staff (u) usable—verify your actual 50 Attack first. But a first solo Waterbirth Dungeon trip involves route/entry risk and a potentially long rare <strong>berserker-ring</strong> chase. The ring is not needed to start Sailing or pass this chapter, so a properly equipped optional Rex primer fits better in the later combat/PvM lane. Nothing here assumes a Rex kill or ring drop.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <section><div class="section-label">Learn Sailing from zero</div><h2>Your boat is a moving workspace, not a teleport menu.</h2><p>Sailing is a new skill with ports, a helm, a cargo hold and one-time exploration tasks. Learn the small core loop before chasing XP rates: take a task or chart target, board, sail, dock, interact, and record the result.</p></section>

      <RouteStep id="i23-pandemonium" number="8" title="Complete Pandemonium and learn the raft controls">
        <p>Speak to <strong>Will and Anne on Port Sarim docks</strong>. Pandemonium has <strong>no skill prerequisite</strong>; play the live quest tutorial rather than using any alpha/beta skip. It teaches boarding and docking. On a ship, walk around the deck normally, then click the <strong>helm</strong> to steer: click a direction around the boat and use the navigation interface's speed arrows to move or reverse; the stop/start toggle pauses motion. Slow down and click a dock's <strong>mooring point</strong>, then use the gangplank to disembark. Your boat remains a persistent vessel you can manage or recover through a <strong>shipwright</strong> at major ports.</p>
        <p>The quest gives <strong>300 Sailing XP</strong> on completion, a <strong>raft</strong>, <strong>Captain's log</strong>, <strong>spyglass</strong>, starter <strong>repair kits</strong> and <strong>wood-plank sawmill coupons</strong>; its guided cargo delivery also gives Sailing practice. Keep the log: its chart and port-task views are your checklist, and another can be reclaimed if lost. The spyglass marks specific distant charting sights. If your hull loses HP, use a repair kit on the ship; reaching zero sends the boat back to the last port rather than killing your character, though normal monster deaths still matter. Ship <strong>facilities</strong> are buildable deck workstations such as hooks or later combat gear; hull, helm and sail upgrades are managed at a shipwright's <strong>Shipyard/schematics board</strong> with tools and materials. You do not need to build them all now. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Pandemonium" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Sailing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki Sailing controls</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-sailing-12" number="9" title="Use early port tasks and charting to reach actual 12 Sailing">
        <p>Start at the <strong>notice board</strong> in Port Sarim or The Pandemonium. A <strong>courier port task</strong> names cargo and a destination: accept it, collect the crate at the origin's ledger table, put it in your boat's <strong>cargo hold</strong>, sail and dock at the destination, unload it at that port's ledger, then claim the reward. At level 1 you can hold one task, rising to two at level 7. The short Port Sarim–Pandemonium trips teach the loop; Musa Point routes open around level 10. Tasks can be cancelled if a route is inconvenient, so no particular random assignment is required.</p>
        <p><strong>Sea charting</strong> is one-time exploration XP, not a repeatable click spot. Open the Captain's log's charts, pick an accessible nearby observation, sail to its marked feature and click/inspect it; for spyglass tasks, use the spyglass from the indicated viewpoint. Some simple targets merely require passing through or interacting with scenery. Claim sea-completion bonuses from <strong>Chartin' Charles McAtless</strong> in the Pandemonium Cave with the log when available. Noticeable ocean encounters or mysterious glows encountered along the way can add XP; treat them as bonuses rather than a fixed quota. Alternate courier deliveries and new chart targets until the skill tab shows <strong>actual 12</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Sea_charting" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki charting task types</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-prying" number="10" title="Complete Prying Times and retain the crowbar">
        <p>Check <strong>Pandemonium complete, actual 12 Sailing and actual 30 Smithing</strong>. The Knight's Sword was completed in <strong>Chapter 1.1</strong>, and 2.2 already took Smithing to 50. Bring your <strong>Captain's log, one steel bar, one redberry pie and a hammer</strong> (the hammer is obtainable during the quest). Leave <strong>one Port Task slot free</strong> before speaking to <strong>“Squawking” Steve Beanie</strong> at The Pandemonium pub; the quest uses a task delivery. Follow his crate/Thurgo errand, deal with or evade the level-14 Drink troll, and finish with Steve. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Prying_Times" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki current quest walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <p>The live quest gives <strong>800 Sailing XP and 1,000 Smithing XP</strong>, <strong>25 oak-plank sawmill coupons</strong>, and access to a <strong>crowbar</strong>. Keep/reclaim the crowbar from the Pandemonium crate as needed: it opens sealed charting objects and the forgotten-drinks charting category, expanding the relaxed one-time XP pool. Do not use pre-launch reward figures.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-sailing-22" number="11" title="Continue ordinary Sailing to actual 22">
        <p>With the crowbar, revisit the Captain's log and clear reachable sealed-crate/forgotten-drink observations while doing convenient courier tasks. At <strong>15 Sailing</strong>, a <strong>skiff</strong> becomes available from a shipwright for <strong>15,000 coins</strong>. It is a larger, more comfortable boat and can take a <strong>salvaging hook</strong>: sail beside a small shipwreck, deploy the hook to recover salvage for XP, store it in the cargo hold, then sort it at a port's salvaging station for more XP and materials. A raft can also be fitted with a hook; the skiff is convenient, not the unlock itself. Buy/fit it if you want variety or a better boat for later; charting and couriers remain valid if the cash or materials would be better saved.</p>
        <p>Use the Captain's log to pick attainable nearby charting, take tasks where they naturally connect ports, and notice ocean encounters without turning every sea tile into a required stop. Reach <strong>actual 22 Sailing</strong>, then do the quest below. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Shipwreck_salvaging" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki salvage loop</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-current-affairs" number="12" title="Complete Current Affairs and learn current charting">
        <p>Check <strong>actual 22 Sailing, 10 Fishing and Pandemonium</strong>; Fishing is already well above the gate. Bring <strong>50 coins</strong>, with <strong>charcoal</strong> if banked (or take it from the Catherby council office), and have your boat at the <strong>Catherby dock</strong>. Speak to <strong>Arhein</strong> there, work through Councillor Catherine's form and the fish-mayor errand, then sail to the nearby current and use Arhein's <strong>current duck</strong> to trace it. This teaches a new charting action rather than requiring guesswork at random ripples. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Current_Affairs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest route</a>.</p>
        <p>Finish with Arhein for <strong>1,400 Sailing XP, 1,000 Fishing XP, the current duck and 25 oak-plank sawmill coupons</strong>. Keep the duck with the charting tools; its current-tracking entries expand the one-time charting pool.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i23-sailing-45" number="13" title="Sail in useful bands to actual 45, then stop">
        <p><strong>22–29:</strong> use the new current-duck entries, leftover crowbar/spyglass observations, convenient courier jobs, and skiff salvage if you built it. The log shows attainable chart targets; collect completed sea bonuses from Charles. Bounty tasks begin at 30, but nothing here requires ship combat or a cannon.</p>
        <p><strong>30–37:</strong> <strong>Barracuda Trials</strong> open at 30—repeatable Sailing obstacle courses in which you steer around hazards and collect cargo under rank conditions. The first, <strong>Tempor Tantrum</strong>, is an active/faster change of pace, not a mandatory grind. To try it, use a skiff equipped with an <strong>iron helm, oak mast and linen sails</strong>; check the live Shipyard schematic before spending resources. One-time rank rewards can be worthwhile, but repeated trials and their timing challenges are not the price of reaching 45. At <strong>31</strong>, a teak hull is a useful skiff speed upgrade; your 2.1 Construction exceeds its level gate, but the hull still consumes materials (roughly <strong>50 teak planks</strong> plus fittings). A shipwright can help with a missing Construction level, <em>not</em> waive materials. If your teak stock is earmarked for later Construction, stay with the current hull and keep charting/couriers instead. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Barracuda_Trials" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki trials</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Shipbuilding" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki ship schematics</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>38–45:</strong> level 38 opens <strong>mermaid-guide</strong> charting; follow the Captain's log's high-30s observations and finish the accessible Ardent/Sunset sea collections for their one-time completion XP. Fill any remaining gap with ordinary courier tasks, charting, salvage or encounters that you enjoy. The published training guide notes that later updates may change individual task lists, so use the <em>live</em> log and level-up interface rather than a fixed coordinate dump or claimed exact XP/hour. Stop only when the skill tab reads <strong>actual 45 Sailing</strong>. No optional trial rank, teak hull or skiff salvage quota is required. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Sailing_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki training bands</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i23-sailing-choices" informational={true} skill="Sailing" target="actual 45" why="45 is the later Troubled Tortugans Sailing gate; the quest's separate 51 Slayer gate is not being pulled forward." recommended="Explore attainable one-time charting with the Captain's log, collecting sea bonuses, and interleave convenient courier tasks; use crowbar and current duck when their entries unlock." relaxed="Add skiff/small-wreck salvage for variety and materials, or stay with couriers if you prefer a predictable port-to-port loop. Neither is a separate checkpoint." fast="Try Tempor Tantrum from 30 with the required skiff fittings for active XP and one-time rank rewards; repeated timed trials are optional." />
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">2.3 exit check</div>
        <h3>The kingdom is running, RFD's lighthouse gate is closed, and Sailing is ready for its later quest.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Throne of Miscellania and Royal Trouble</strong> complete; kingdom funded, approval checked periodically and all 15 workers assigned (default ten herbs + five teaks, adjusted for your bank).</li>
          <li><strong>Actual 40+ Slayer</strong> verified. Record the real level after Royal Trouble's 5,000 Slayer XP; do not infer a hidden 50/51.</li>
          <li><strong>Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl and Horror from the Deep</strong> complete before 2.4's Recipe for Disaster. Damaged god book retained; pages and optional combat detours are not required.</li>
          <li><strong>Pandemonium, Prying Times and Current Affairs</strong> complete; actual <strong>45 Sailing</strong> verified. Keep the boat, Captain's log, spyglass, crowbar, current duck and repair supplies accessible.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Troubled Tortugans is deliberately postponed.</strong> Sailing is ready, and the route already covers its 48 Construction, 45 Hunter, 40 Woodcutting and 34 Crafting gates, but it requires <strong>actual 51 Slayer</strong>. The later Morytania/Slayer block will raise 40 → 50 → 51 and then reopen Sailing. Neither optional Chapter 1 melee, Barbarian Assault nor Dagannoth Rex is assumed.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="subchapter-pager"><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/`}>← 2.2</a><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}intermediate/`}>Back to Intermediate overview</a></div>
